{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Validate and Generate Test Cases",
  "description": "Manually trigger to invoke QA-Validator-Agent after Expert phase is complete. Also triggered by renaming test_plan to _OK.md suffix.",
  "version": "5",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Validator-Agent.\n\nAsk the user: **Which ticket folder?** (e.g., '2026/Q1/Version 227/PROJ-1234 - POS Start of Day - Print Forecast by Hour')\n\nOnce they provide the path:\n\n1. **CHECK FOR EXISTING TEST CASES** in 2_Validator/:\n   - If `FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_PENDING.md` or `FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_OK.md` exists, read it FIRST\n   - Extract the `## QA Comments` section (everything between `## QA Comments` and the next `##` heading)\n   - These comments are MANDATORY inputs — they override all other sources\n\n2. **READ INPUTS** from 1_Expert/ folder:\n   - test_plan_*.md (the test plan)\n   - manual_input.md (human observations, if filled)\n   - logic_explanation.md (full context)\n\n3. **APPLY STANDARDS**:\n   - Read @TestCasesDesign.md for formatting standards\n   - Merge all sources with this priority: QA Comments > manual_input > test_plan > logic_explanation\n   - Rewrite all test cases into required format\n   - Preserve the `## QA Comments` section at the top of the output WITH its content intact (never clear it — comments persist across regenerations)\n\n4. **WRITE OUTPUT** — ALWAYS overwrite the SAME file:\n   - Find the existing `FINAL_TEST_CASES_*` file in 2_Validator/ and overwrite it IN PLACE using the EXACT same filename\n   - NEVER create a new file. NEVER generate a second file. NEVER change the filename.\n   - Use a single fsWrite call to the EXACT same path that already exists\n   - If no file exists yet (first generation), use: `2_Validator/FINAL_TEST_CASES_{TICKET_ID}_PENDING.md`\n   - Optionally save `2_Validator/FINAL_QA_SUMMARY.md`\n\n5. **MANDATORY POST-REVISION INTEGRITY CHECK** (from @qa-validator-workflow.md):\n   Before writing the final output, verify:\n   - (a) Count all TCs from source inputs vs your output — every TC from the test plan must appear unless explicitly excluded by QA Comments\n   - (b) TC IDs are sequential with NO gaps (TC-001, TC-002, ..., TC-NNN)\n   - (c) Every TC has ALL required sections: header, Priority, Test Type, Automation Status, Regression Potential, Source, Preconditions (bullet list), Test Steps (numbered with Expected per step), Expected Result, Test Data\n   - (d) Test Summary Matrix rows match detailed TC sections 1:1 — same count, same IDs, same titles\n   - (e) Add a revision comment block documenting changes made and before/after TC count\n   - If a TC cannot be recovered from sources, flag with <!-- MISSING --> comment\n\nThe output file MUST start with:\n```\n# {TICKET_ID} — {Title}\n\n## QA Comments\n<!-- QA: Write feedback, corrections, or change requests here. These override all other inputs on next regeneration. -->\n{existing QA comments preserved here}\n\n## Test Summary Matrix\n...\n```\n\n⚠️ CRITICAL: ALWAYS OVERWRITE THE EXISTING FILE. Same path, same filename. Do NOT create FINAL_TEST_CASES_*_PENDING_2.md or any variant. One file, always overwritten.\n\nFollow @context_efficiency.md rules. Write only to 2_Validator/. Stop after saving.\n\nERROR RECOVERY: If any step fails (missing input files, format error, write failure), write a file named `VALIDATOR_ERROR.md` at the ticket root with: the step that failed, the error message, and what was completed successfully. Then STOP."
  }
}
